3D Spacetime diagrams\
\
GOALS : \
Create a single-file interactive html page using three.js and JavaScript that shows various spacetime diagrams and examples. Diagrams and examples should have various controls that change aspects and quantities.\
\
1: Model gravitational redshift. Visually show how electromagnetic radiation redshifts while moving from an area near mass to an area away from mass. Use Schwarzschild metric. Assume the viewers frame of reference is at infinity. Provide a few different options for the warping of spacetime; one as a deforming and stretching cubic grid (see reference Spacetime_warp_3D_grid.png in docs), another as Visualize the warping of spacetime as \
\
\
1: A sphere that represents the observable universe. Attributes include\
- the center is earth, the outer edge is recombination, ie the moment that the CMB photons could flow freely through the universe\
- the center is the present moment, ie the full age of the universe, the outer edge is 380,000 years after the big bang\
- this diagram represents a spherical coordinate slice of our 4D\'92 light cone\'92 of our frame of reference. with distance from the center equal to time since the big bang\
\
Questions\
Does a light beam, emitted inside a dense fog, redshift from point A to point B, if the fog is rapidly expanding? ie becoming less dense? Or becoming more condensed in specific areas, just not around around the light beam?\
